  JMM in 5 Rules (B T T P P)  
  { Box / Total / Thread / Publication / Program Order }
============================================================================================

 _______________________________________    ----------> Acquire Semantics (Monitor Enter)
|					|
|					|   Instr X
|					|
|_______________________________________|
                                            ----------> Release Semantics (Monitor Exit)


<1> Box: 
    -> Check in but cant check out
    -> Acquire / Volatile load represent top of  box 
    -> Release / Volatile store represent bottom of box
    -> For arch with weak or non coherent caches
       ----> MeN requires acquire barrier (aka dont return following reads w/o checking with
             main memory)
       ----> MeX requires flushing local store buffers and pushing writes to point of coherence


<2> Total Lock / Total Volatile Store order
    Cant reoder these


<3> Thread start has MeN and Thread join has MeX semantics


<4> Publication Safety:
    -> final stores not reordered with stores outside ctor function
    -> If ctor inlined stores on object reference not reordered with final field stores

    [Keep in mind non final fields are not guaranteed to be *not* reordered]
    [Also another reason why this should not escape until ctor completes else escaped
     ref may not see all final writes]


<5> Reads maintain program order for local stores


